Q: Select all text of TextField in Jetpack Compose A: <p>I modified the codes of <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/users/95482/tom-berghuis">Tom Berghuis</a> and made it a new Modifier extended function. No need to use delay(50) or something like that.</p>
<pre><code>import androidx.compose.runtime.LaunchedEffect
import androidx.compose.runtime.MutableState
import androidx.compose.runtime.getValue
import androidx.compose.runtime.mutableStateOf
import androidx.compose.runtime.remember
import androidx.compose.runtime.setValue
import androidx.compose.ui.Modifier
import androidx.compose.ui.composed
import androidx.compose.ui.focus.onFocusChanged
import androidx.compose.ui.text.TextRange
import androidx.compose.ui.text.input.TextFieldValue

fun Modifier.onFocusSelectAll(
    textState: MutableState&lt;TextFieldValue&gt;,
    runOnlyOnce: Boolean = false
): Modifier = composed {
    var triggered by remember { mutableStateOf(false) }
    var triggerEffect by remember { mutableStateOf(false) }

    var triggerCount by remember { mutableStateOf(0) }

    val focusModifier = Modifier.onFocusChanged { focusState -&gt;
        if (focusState.isFocused) {
            triggerCount++

            if (!runOnlyOnce || !triggered) {
                triggered = true
                triggerEffect = !triggerEffect 
            }
        }
    }

    /* We can take advantage of LaunchedEffect function 100% in this case.
      At any Composable it runs anyway at first, but it is blocked by triggerCount.
      It will be run when a user get a focus in the BasicTextField, 
      which increase triggerCount and toggles tiggerEffect.
      As long as a user stays in the textfield editing something, no selection can not occur.
      runOnlyOnce variable is useful when you don't want select again staying in the same screen.
      But usually whenever we try to key in something like 2-digits numbers, 
      it is better to select all the values of the textfield in order to put the number directly 
      deleting the old values without backspace keys.  
    */
    LaunchedEffect(triggerEffect) {
        if (triggerCount &gt; 0) {
            val current = textState.value
            textState.value = current.copy(
                selection = TextRange(0, current.text.length)
            )
        }
    }

    this.then(focusModifier)
}



/*  How to use the extention function
@Composable
fun SelectAllModifierDemo() {
    val state = remember { mutableStateOf(TextFieldValue(&quot;initial text&quot;)) }

    BasicTextField(
        value = state.value,
        onValueChange = { state.value = it },
        modifier = Modifier.onFocusSelectAll(state, runOnlyOnce = false)
    )
}
*/
</code></pre>

Q: Need help creating a custom ListBox in C# WinForms (Visual Studio 2022) A: <p>Set the <code>DrawMode</code> to <code>OwnerDrawFixed</code> and override <code>OnDrawItem</code> where you put your drawing logic.</p>
<p>Here is an example of a <code>ListBox</code> displaying font names along with a font example:</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>public class FontFamilyListBox : ListBox
{
    public FontFamilyListBox()
    {
        IntegralHeight = false;
        SelectionMode = SelectionMode.One;
        ItemHeight = Math.Max(ItemHeight, 18);
        Height = 16 * ItemHeight + 3;
        DrawMode = DrawMode.OwnerDrawFixed;

        foreach (var family in FontFamily.Families) {
            Items.Add(family.Name);
        }
    }

    protected override void OnDrawItem(DrawItemEventArgs e)
    {
        const string ExampleText = &quot;Abc 123&quot;;

        string fontFamilyName = (string)Items[e.Index];
        using var itemFont = new Font(fontFamilyName, 12);
        using var brush = new SolidBrush(e.ForeColor);
        e.DrawBackground();
        e.Graphics.DrawString(itemFont.Name, Font, brush, e.Bounds.X, e.Bounds.Y);

        float textWidth = e.Graphics.MeasureString(itemFont.Name, Font).Width;
        float exampleWidth = e.Graphics.MeasureString(ExampleText, itemFont).Width;
        if (textWidth + exampleWidth + 3 &lt; e.Bounds.Width) {
            e.Graphics.DrawString(ExampleText, itemFont, brush, e.Bounds.Right - exampleWidth - 1, e.Bounds.Y);
        }
        e.DrawFocusRectangle();
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p><a href="https://i.sstatic.net/7olsuoqe.png" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><img src="https://i.sstatic.net/7olsuoqe.png" alt="enter image description here" /></a>.</p>
<p>This code could be improved by using <code>DrawMode</code> <code>OwnerDrawVariable</code> and adapting the item height according to the measured height of the font example.</p>
<p>You can find the <a href="https://github.com/OJacot-Descombes/PrettyDocComments/blob/master/PrettyDocComments/CustomOptions/Design/FontFamilyListBox.cs" rel="nofollow noreferrer">original code on my GitHub</a></p>
